1a:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-amber-200 text-gray-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Your task: "}],"Learn the sequences, because doffing is where contamination actually happens."]}]
1b:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"PPE is selected by the task and the expected exposure, not by habit. Gloves for contact with blood, body fluids, mucous membranes, or non-intact skin. A gown when clothing may be soiled. A mask and eye protection when splashes or sprays are possible. A respirator rather than a mask for airborne pathogens."}]
1c:["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Donning — put on"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Doffing — take off"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"1. Gown"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"1. Gloves"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"2. Mask or respirator"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"2. Eye protection"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"3. Eye protection"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"3. Gown"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"4. Gloves — over the gown cuffs"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"4. Mask or respirator — last, and outside the room"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Donning and doffing sequences"}]]}]
1d:["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Doffing is the highest-risk moment in the entire sequence, because everything you are removing is contaminated on the outside. Gloves come off first because they are the most contaminated. The mask comes off last because it protects you while you handle everything else, and it is removed by its ties or ear loops — never by touching the front. Hand hygiene follows immediately, and is also performed between steps if you contaminate your hands."]}]
1e:["$","figure","4",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Type"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"For"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Requires"}],["$","th","3",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Examples"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Contact"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Spread by direct or indirect touch"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Gown and gloves; dedicated equipment"}],["$","td","3",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"C. difficile, MRSA, scabies"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Droplet"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Spread by respiratory droplets over short distances"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Surgical mask; patient masked during transport"}],["$","td","3",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Influenza, pertussis, mumps"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Airborne"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Spread by small particles that remain suspended"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"N95 or higher respirator, fit-tested; negative-pressure room"}],["$","td","3",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Tuberculosis, measles, varicella"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Transmission-based precautions"}]]}]
1f:["$","p","5",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Transmission-based precautions are applied in addition to Standard Precautions, never instead of them. Some conditions require more than one type — varicella requires both airborne and contact precautions, for example."}]
20:["$","div","6",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"A surgical mask and an N95 respirator are not interchangeable. A surgical mask blocks large droplets and protects the patient from you. An N95 filters small airborne particles and protects you — but only if it is fit-tested to your face and you have passed a seal check. An unfitted N95 provides substantially less protection than its rating suggests, which is why fit testing is a requirement rather than a formality."]}]
21:["$","$L25","7",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Why are gloves removed first when doffing PPE?","options":["They are the easiest item to remove","They are the most contaminated, so removing them first prevents transferring contamination to everything else","They must be removed before hand hygiene can be performed","It is arbitrary, as long as hand hygiene follows"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"The doffing sequence works from most contaminated to least. Gloves have had the most direct contact with contaminated surfaces, so removing them first prevents them from transferring contamination to your gown, eye protection, face, and mask as you continue.","optionRationales":["Ease is not the principle. The sequence follows the degree of contamination.","Correct. Most contaminated comes off first so it cannot spread to the rest.","Hand hygiene is performed after glove removal, but that is a consequence of the order rather than its reason.","The sequence is not arbitrary — it is specifically designed to prevent self-contamination during removal."]}}]
22:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-[40px] sm:leading-[1.05]","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"PPE technique is a psychomotor skill. Reading about it is preparation for practicing it under supervision, not a substitute."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find the CDC's PPE donning and doffing sequence poster. Write both sequences from memory, then check."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"For each scenario, list the PPE required: a routine blood draw; assisting with a procedure where splashing is likely; caring for a patient on contact precautions; entering the room of a patient with suspected tuberculosis."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Research what an N95 fit test involves and why it must be repeated periodically."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Practice the doffing sequence with any substitute materials you have. Identify the two points where you were most likely to contaminate yourself."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
